        "description": "Normal or minimally abnormal fundus appearance without typical signs of cone dystrophy",
        "category": "supportive",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      },
      {
        "id": "genetic-testing",
        "description": "Identification of pathogenic variants in genes associated with cone function (e.g., CNGA3, CNGB3)",
        "category": "supportive",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      }
    ],
    "minimumForDiagnosis": "Presence of reduced cone function with preserved rod function on ERG combined with near normal color vision",
    "notes": "Diagnosis is primarily clinical and electrophysiological; genetic testing can support diagnosis but is not mandatory."
